OmacVM Cocoa: the tiled present also when frames are shown when drawn

What: "Draw only what changed" (OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_TILES, ADR 0055) ran only
with the vsync present; with OMACVM_GL_VSYNC=0 (frames shown as soon as the
GPU is done) it said "off (needs the vsync present)". Now a tile frame shown
when drawn goes on the layers on the main queue, as the whole frames there
do, so both kinds reach the layers in the order they were drawn; a whole
frame shown when drawn hides the tiles and measures whether later frames may
go in tiles, through the same helper as the vsync present's whole frames
(present_tiles_whole_shown). present_bh is made in both modes: it asks for
a whole frame after the tiles hid and draws the newest frame when the window
is seen again. The vsync present (the default) does exactly what it did.

Why: a hidden test window (OMACVM_COCOA_HIDDEN) is never ordered in, so its
display link never ticks and the vsync present shows its first frames and
then none: no tiles check could run there, and the tiles + partial present
check needed a window on a display (present-locked.sh's virtual display, or
a person's screen). Frames shown when drawn need no tick, so tiles and the
partial present (ADR 0051) run together in check mode on a hidden window,
also on a Mac where no row may make a virtual display.

Upstream: OmacVM only (the tiled present is ours).
Tests: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-present-tiles-direct.sh (wiring, and
--self-test: every check fails without this patch); rows: hidden mini rows
with OMACVM_GL_VSYNC=0, OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_TILES=check and
OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_DAMAGE=check, and the half-box fault
(work/power-1117/tiles-rects).

